halogen: KV budget 4 slot(s) over one 524288-position pool (each request up to 262144) = 14.9 GiB (~28 KiB/position incl. block scratch + ~115 MiB/slot) + 2.7 GiB prompt cache in RAM, on top of roughly 72 GiB (an 8-bit GGUF trunk, file type 30, repacked into RAM) of weights and 12.6 GiB of working memory (HALOGEN_MAX_TOK 32768). Those last two are estimates for this pre-flight check; the engine prints its measured figures once loaded, including the large lookup table it reads from disk and never holds. MemAvailable now 112.9 GiB.
halogen: WARNING: that budget is close to or over what this host has free (the engine refuses the last pin under 16 GiB of MemAvailable).
  If startup ends in "checkpoint: refusing to pin" or "HIP ... out of memory", lower HALOGEN_MAX_TOK to 16384 (the working memory, about 4 GiB back on the default checkpoint and 1.6 on w4b, for about 9% of prefill speed)
  or HALOGEN_KV_POOL_POSITIONS (the pool, ~29.5 KiB a position); a 1,048,576-position pool fits only with HALOGEN_MAX_TOK=16384.
